: of all the largest ones, the lexicographically least by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex index, in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order; [] for the empty graph. Of two sets of one size, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lesser holds the least vertex of their symmetric difference (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximumClique()"},{"text":"’s rule, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on a loop-free graph this is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximumClique()"},{"text":" of the complement). A vertex with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"self-loop is never in it; parallel edges count once.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"maximumIndependentSet()","role":"symbol"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/minimumEdgeCover()":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumEdgeCover"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":"]?"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A minimum edge cover (positions, ascending), or nil when some vertex has no edge: the edges of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximumMatching()"},{"text":", then for each vertex still uncovered, in vertex order, its first edge in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges"},{"text":" order (a self-loop covers its vertex). n − ν edges (Gallai).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O(n · m · log n).","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"minimumEdgeCover()","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumedgecover()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumEdgeCover()"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/approximateMinimumDominatingSet(weight:)-6gboe":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"approximateMinimumDominatingSet"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/approximateminimumdominatingset(weight:)-6gboe","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/approximateMinimumDominatingSet(weight:)-6gboe","abstract":[{"text":"A dominating set of at most H(Δ + 1) times the least weight (Chvátal’s greedy set cover;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"NetworkX ","type":"text"},{"code":"min_weighted_dominating_set","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the same set): repeatedly the vertex with the least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"weight per newly dominated vertex of its closed neighbourhood, the least vertex index on ties.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Ratios are compared exactly, by cross-multiplication. ","type":"text"},{"code":"weight","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is called once per vertex.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O((n + m) log n).","type":"text"}],"title":"approximateMinimumDominatingSet(weight:)","role":"symbol"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/maximalIndependentSet(containing:)":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maximalIndependentSet","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"containing","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sequence","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">) -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]?","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A maximal independent set containing ","type":"text"},{"code":"seeds","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which go in first, then each vertex in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order as ","type":"text"},{"code":"maximalIndependentSet()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; nil when "},{"code":"seeds","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is not an independent set"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(two are adjacent, or one has a self-loop). Repeats are one seed. O(n + m)."}],"type":"topic","title":"maximalIndependentSet(containing:)","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximalindependentset(containing:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximalIndependentSet(containing:)"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/minimumVertexCover(bipartition:)":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumVertexCover","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"bipartition","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bipartition","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:15BipartiteGraphs11BipartitionV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">) -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumVertexCover(bipartition:)","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumvertexcover(bipartition:)","abstract":[{"text":"König’s minimum vertex cover of a bipartite graph (NetworkX ","type":"text"},{"code":"to_vertex_cover","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cover): from a maximum matching (Hopcroft–Karp on the sides), Z is the set of vertices","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reached from the free left vertices by alternating paths, an edge not in the matching from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"left to right, then the matched edge back; the cover is (left ∖ Z) ∪ (right ∩ Z), in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order. It is the one minimum cover with the most left vertices, so it does not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"depend on the matching. O(m √n).","type":"text"}],"title":"minimumVertexCover(bipartition:)","role":"symbol"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/approximateMinimumVertexCover(weight:)":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"approximateMinimumVertexCover","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A vertex cover of at most twice the least weight (Bar-Yehuda and Even’s local ratio; NetworkX"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"min_weighted_vertex_cover","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the same cover when positions are in its edge order): each edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in position order with neither end in the cover puts in the end with the lesser remaining"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"weight (the end with the lesser vertex index on ties) and subtracts that weight from the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other end’s. A self-loop puts its vertex in. ","type":"text"},{"code":"weight","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is called once per vertex, in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order. O(n + m).","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"approximateMinimumVertexCover(weight:)","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/approximateminimumvertexcover(weight:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/approximateMinimumVertexCover(weight:)"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/minimumVertexCover()":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumVertexCover"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumvertexcover()","abstract":[{"text":"A minimum vertex cover (exact): ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" minus ","type":"text"},{"code":"maximumIndependentSet()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order (τ = n − α, Gallai), so the minimum cover avoiding the least vertex of a symmetric"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"difference. Every vertex with a self-loop is in it; parallel edges count once. The cost is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"maximumIndependentSet()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s: O(m √n) on bipartite components."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumVertexCover()","title":"minimumVertexCover()","role":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"An undirected graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of undirected edges","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"between them. Kept apart from ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": an undirected graph is not a symmetric directed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one, and no type is both. ","type":"text"},{"code":"directed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" views it as one when an algorithm needs arcs.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"Graph","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","title":"Graph","role":"symbol"}}}